course: dictionary
lesson: 2465
title: Light, dark and the word darkness
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Darkness is a noun. It means little or no light. «In total darkness we see nothing at all.» Dark is the adjective, and darkness is the thing itself: the dark room, the darkness of the room.
explain: We can only see when light enters our eyes. When the light is gone, our eyes have nothing to catch. «The night sky is dark although there are countless stars» shows that even at night, a lot of the sky is empty darkness between the stars.
explain: Writers also use darkness to mean evil or sadness. In a story, «the darkness of night» may be a real night, but it can also make readers feel afraid or uneasy. Look at the words around it to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: Darkness means little or no light.
fact: «Total darkness» means there is no light at all.
fact: Darkness is uncountable: we say «some darkness» or «the darkness», not «two darknesses».
fact: In stories, darkness can mean evil or sadness.
fact: Mexican tetra fish trapped in dark caves lost their eyes, because eyes are useless in darkness and cost energy.
exercise: «A boy walking home in winter darkness wore a reflective band.» What does darkness mean here? | *Little or no light | Very hot weather | A friendly dog | Heavy rain
exercise: «Owls cannot see in total darkness.» What is total darkness in this sentence? | Clouds in the sky | *No light at all | Very bright sunshine | A small light
exercise: In a story, the words «a cold darkness filled her heart» most likely mean? | Lots of rain | A sunny day | Tidying up the room | *Sadness or fear
test: Why can't we see in total darkness? | Because the stars are too far away | Because darkness makes us sleepy | Because our eyes are always closed | *Because no light enters our eyes
test: Which word is the noun for the state of being dark? | *darkness | dark | darken | darkly
exam: Which sentence uses darkness to mean evil or sadness, not just no light? | «The lamp gave a warm glow in the room.» | *«The book's darkness made the readers feel uneasy.» | «The fish swam in the dark river.» | «Owls cannot see in total darkness.»
